  {
    "id": "seo",
    "title": "SEO",
    "body": "# SEO\n\nThe SEO suite: site metrics, competitors, tracked keywords and alerts, content gaps,\ninternal links, LLM mentions, engagement, backlinks, the disavow list and link\nopportunities. Reads and curation are free; the seven scans marked `x-spends-credits` or\n`x-spends-money` cost money and always need a person's approval when an AI agent asks.\n\n## GET /seo/overview\n\nRead the SEO overview\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getSeoOverview\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe latest site metrics for the Site's own domain and each tracked competitor (domain rank,\nestimated organic traffic, ranking keywords by position band, backlinks and referring domains),\nplus the own site's 90-day trend. Free to read; refreshing costs credits\n(`POST /seo/site-metrics/refresh`). A null snapshot means never measured, not zero.\n\n## POST /seo/site-metrics/refresh\n\nRefresh the site metrics\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: yes.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"refreshSiteMetrics\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nMeasure the Site's own domain and its tracked competitors again now, rather than at the weekly\nrefresh.\n\nIt spends about 12 credits. It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`getSeoOverview`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A site metrics scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), a primary domain (`PATCH /site/settings`) (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /seo/competitors\n\nList competitors\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listCompetitors\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe competitors the SEO suite tracks for this Site, and the Site's own domain (`is_own_site`).\nContent gap, backlink and intersect scans compare against the active ones.\n\n## POST /seo/competitors\n\nTrack a competitor\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"addCompetitor\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nAdd a competitor domain to track. Free: nothing is measured until a scan runs. At most 25 active\ncompetitors per Site (`422` on `domain` beyond that); the Site's own domain is `422`; a domain\nalready tracked is `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## PATCH /seo/competitors/{id}\n\nChange a competitor\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateCompetitor\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRename a competitor or pause it (`is_active: false`), which leaves it out of scans without losing\nits history. The Site's own row is `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## DELETE /seo/competitors/{id}\n\nStop tracking a competitor\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"removeCompetitor\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRemove a competitor and its measured history. To keep the history, pause it instead with\n`PATCH /seo/competitors/{id}`. The Site's own row is `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## GET /seo/keywords\n\nList tracked keywords\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listTrackedKeywords\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe keywords whose Google position is tracked for this Site, priority first, with the latest\nposition. `latest_position` null means not ranking in the top 100, or not checked yet\n(`latest_checked_at` null).\n\n## POST /seo/keywords\n\nTrack a keyword\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"trackKeyword\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nStart tracking a keyword. Free: adding makes no vendor call, and positions arrive with the next\nrank check. Location and language default to the Site's locale.\n\nThe plan limits how many keywords the organisation tracks across all its Sites; past it is\n`402 NOT_ENTITLED` (\"Your plan tracks up to N keywords across the organisation.\"). A keyword\nalready tracked is `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## PATCH /seo/keywords/{id}\n\nChange a tracked keyword\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateTrackedKeyword\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nMark a keyword as a priority (checked daily rather than weekly), set the page that should rank\nfor it, or pause it. Re-activating checks the plan's keyword limit again (`402 NOT_ENTITLED`).\n\n## DELETE /seo/keywords/{id}\n\nStop tracking a keyword\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"untrackKeyword\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nStop tracking a keyword. Its position history and alerts are deleted with it; to keep them,\npause it with `PATCH /seo/keywords/{id}` instead.\n\n## GET /seo/keywords/{id}/history\n\nRead a keyword's position history\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getKeywordHistory\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe keyword's recorded positions, newest first, with search volume and, where Search Console\nprovides them, impressions and clicks.\n\n## GET /seo/keyword-alerts\n\nList keyword alerts\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listKeywordAlerts\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nPosition changes worth a look (a keyword entering or leaving the top 10, a large drop), newest\nfirst. Unacknowledged ones by default.\n\n## POST /seo/keyword-alerts/acknowledge\n\nAcknowledge keyword alerts\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"acknowledgeKeywordAlerts\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nMark alerts as seen: send `ids` (up to 100) or `all: true`, not both. Acknowledged alerts stay\nreadable with `?acknowledged=true`.\n\n## POST /seo/rank-check\n\nCheck keyword positions now\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"runRankCheck\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nCheck the Google position of every active tracked keyword now, rather than at the weekly (daily\nfor priority keywords) check.\n\nIt spends no credits, but it costs Writavo a vendor fee per keyword, so it is treated as spending money. It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`listTrackedKeywords`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A rank check scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), at least one active tracked keyword (`POST /seo/keywords`) (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /seo/content-gaps\n\nList content gaps\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listContentGaps\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nKeywords competitors rank for and this Site does not, best opportunity first. Plan one into the\ncontent plan with `POST /seo/content-gaps/{id}/plan`, or dismiss it.\n\n## POST /seo/content-gaps/scan\n\nScan for content gaps\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: yes.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"scanContentGaps\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nCompare the Site's ranking keywords with each active competitor's and record the gaps.\n\nIt spends about one `seo.content_gap_scan` charge per active competitor (at most 10). It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`listContentGaps`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A content gap scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), a primary domain and at least one active competitor (`POST /seo/competitors`) (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## PATCH /seo/content-gaps/{id}\n\nDismiss or reopen a content gap\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateContentGap\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nSet a gap to `dismissed` (not interesting) or back to `open`. `planned` is set only by\n`POST /seo/content-gaps/{id}/plan`, and a gap already planned is `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## POST /seo/content-gaps/{id}/plan\n\nPlan an article from a content gap\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"planContentGap\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nAdd the gap's keyword to the content plan (`source: content_gap`) and mark the gap `planned`, in\none step. Needs both `seo:write` and `plan:write`. A gap that is not `open` is `409 CONFLICT`.\nWhile the pipeline is on, the planned topic is written (and spends credits) at the next tick.\n\n## GET /seo/internal-links\n\nRead internal link health\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getInternalLinkHealth\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nHow the Site's articles link to each other: the number of internal links, the broken ones (with\nthe article they are in), orphan articles nothing links to, and the most used anchor texts.\n\n## POST /seo/internal-links/rescan\n\nRescan internal links\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"rescanInternalLinks\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRe-read every published article's internal links now. Free (it only reads the Site's own\narticles). Returns `202`; `GET /seo/internal-links` shows the result a few minutes later.\n\n## GET /seo/llm-mentions\n\nList LLM mentions\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listLlmMentions\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nWhether AI answer engines mention or cite the Site for its topics, newest check first. A trend\nsignal, not a guarantee: coverage varies by engine and topic.\n\n## POST /seo/llm-mentions/check\n\nCheck LLM mentions now\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: yes.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"checkLlmMentions\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nAsk the AI answer engines about the Site's topics now and record whether they mention or cite it.\n\nIt spends about up to 20 `seo.ai_overview_check` charges. It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`listLlmMentions`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A LLM mention scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), a primary domain (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /seo/engagement\n\nRead blog engagement\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getEngagement\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nViews, reactions and shares on the published blog, by day and by post, for a date range (the\nlast 30 days by default, at most 366 days). Counted without identifying readers.\n\n## GET /seo/backlinks/overview\n\nRead the backlink overview\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getBacklinkOverview\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe Site's backlink profile in one read: the latest summary for its own domain and each\ncompetitor, a 180-day trend, the top anchors, counts of live, lost, broken and toxic links, where\nthe data came from, the last import, and `paid_data_available`, which says whether the paid scans\ncan run at all. Authority is the data provider's own 0 to 100 rank, not DR or DA; it is null\nwhen the data came from a free source.\n\n## GET /seo/backlinks\n\nList backlinks\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listBacklinks\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nIndividual links pointing at the Site's own domain (the default) or a tracked competitor, highest\nauthority first. `filter` narrows to `live`, `lost`, `broken` or `toxic` links. A domain that is\nneither the Site's nor a tracked competitor is `404`. `is_dofollow` null means not yet verified.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/scan\n\nScan the backlink profile\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: yes.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"scanBacklinkProfile\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRefresh the backlink profile summary for the Site's own domain and each active competitor now,\nrather than at the weekly refresh.\n\nIt spends about one `seo.backlink_scan` charge per domain (the Site plus up to 10 competitors). It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`getBacklinkOverview`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A backlink profile scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), a primary domain (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\nPaid backlink data is switched off platform wide while `paid_data_available` is false in `GET /seo/backlinks/overview`; then this is `409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE`. The free alternatives are `POST /seo/backlinks/import` (a Search Console links export) and the Bing Webmaster Tools feed.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/detail-pull\n\nPull a page of backlink detail\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: yes.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"pullBacklinkDetail\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nFetch one page of 1,000 individual links for the Site's own domain or a tracked competitor\n(`target_domain`; anything else is `404`). Use `offset` (a multiple of 1,000) for the next page.\n\nIt spends about one `seo.backlink_report` charge (one 1,000 row page). It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`listBacklinks`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A backlink detail scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), a primary domain (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\nPaid backlink data is switched off platform wide while `paid_data_available` is false in `GET /seo/backlinks/overview`; then this is `409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE`. The free alternatives are `POST /seo/backlinks/import` (a Search Console links export) and the Bing Webmaster Tools feed.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /seo/backlinks/disavow\n\nList disavow entries\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listDisavowEntries\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe domains and URLs on this Site's disavow list, newest first. The list only matters once it is\nuploaded to Google Search Console (`GET /seo/backlinks/disavow-file` builds the file), and\nGoogle advises disavowing only links that are clearly harmful.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/disavow\n\nAdd a disavow entry\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"addDisavowEntry\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nAdd a domain or a URL to the disavow list. Nothing is sent to Google: a person uploads the file\nfrom `GET /seo/backlinks/disavow-file` to Search Console. An entry already listed is\n`409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## DELETE /seo/backlinks/disavow/{id}\n\nRemove a disavow entry\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"removeDisavowEntry\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nTake a domain or URL off the disavow list. Google is not told until a person uploads the new\nfile.\n\n## GET /seo/backlinks/disavow-file\n\nBuild the disavow file\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getDisavowFile\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe disavow list as the text file Google Search Console accepts. Free. A person uploads it in\nSearch Console; Writavo never submits it.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/import\n\nImport a Search Console links export\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"importBacklinksCsv\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nImport backlinks from a Google Search Console links export (the \"Top linking pages\" or per-link\nCSV), the free way to fill the backlink profile. Send the CSV text in `csv`, at most 900,000\ncharacters per request: split a larger export into several requests, which is safe because rows\nare matched on the link and never duplicated.\n\nNo primary domain is `409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`. The wrong export is `422` on `csv` (\"This is not a\nSearch Console links export.\"), naming the export needed.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/verify\n\nVerify backlinks\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"verifyBacklinks\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nFetch each known linking page and check the link is still there, whether it is followed, and\nwhether it is broken. Free. Returns `202`; `GET /seo/backlinks/overview` shows the result.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/bing\n\nGet the link to connect Bing Webmaster Tools\n\nScope: integrations:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"connectBing\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nReturns the dashboard page where a person connects Bing Webmaster Tools, the free automated\nbacklink feed. It connects nothing itself: the Bing API key never passes through an AI assistant\nor this API. Give the person `connect_url`; once they say it is done, `POST /seo/backlinks/bing/sync`\nreads the links.\n\n## POST /seo/backlinks/bing/sync\n\nRead backlinks from Bing now\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"syncBing\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRead the latest backlinks from the connected Bing Webmaster Tools account now, rather than at the\nweekly sync. Free. Returns `202`. Not connected is `409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING` naming\n`connect_bing`.\n\n## GET /seo/link-opportunities\n\nList link opportunities\n\nScope: seo:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listLinkOpportunities\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nSites worth getting a link from, best first: found by the competitor intersect scan (they link\nto several competitors but not to this Site) or added by hand. Filter by `status`.\n\n## POST /seo/link-opportunities\n\nAdd a link opportunity\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"addLinkOpportunity\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nAdd a site worth getting a link from, by hand. Free.\n\n## PATCH /seo/link-opportunities/{id}\n\nChange a link opportunity\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateLinkOpportunity\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRecord progress (`contacted`, `won`, `dismissed`, or back to `open`) or a note. `planned` is set\nonly by `POST /seo/link-opportunities/{id}/plan`.\n\n## POST /seo/link-opportunities/{id}/plan\n\nPlan an article for a link opportunity\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"planLinkOpportunity\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nAdd a topic to the content plan (`source: link_opportunity`, \"A resource worth linking to for\n<domain>\") and mark the opportunity `planned`, in one step: the usual way to earn a link is an\narticle worth linking to. Needs both `seo:write` and `plan:write`. Only an `open` or `contacted`\nopportunity; otherwise `409 CONFLICT`.\n\n## POST /seo/link-opportunities/intersect-scan\n\nFind sites that link to competitors\n\nScope: seo:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: yes.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"scanLinkIntersect\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nFind sites that link to two or more of the Site's active competitors but not to the Site, and\nadd them to the link opportunities board. A re-scan never overwrites what a person has already\nrecorded on an opportunity.\n\nIt spends about one `seo.link_intersect` charge per active competitor. It runs in the background: the response is `202` with `queued: true` and\n`estimated_credits`, and `check` names the operation that shows the result a few minutes later\n(`listLinkOpportunities`). A second request of the same kind within 10 minutes is `409 CONFLICT`. That guard is per\nscan kind (\"A link intersect scan is already running.\"), and every page of a detail pull counts.\n\nWhile the organisation's plan has no daily spend cap configured, spending is paused and this is\n`409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE` (\"Spending is paused: this plan has no daily spend cap configured...\");\nnothing on the caller's side fixes it, so report it rather than retry.\n\nChecked in this order, each answered before anything is spent: the plan\n(`402 NOT_ENTITLED`), a primary domain and at least two active competitors (`POST /seo/competitors`) (`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, naming the operation that sets it\nup), credits (`402 INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`) and the Site's spend cap (`402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`).\n\nPaid backlink data is switched off platform wide while `paid_data_available` is false in `GET /seo/backlinks/overview`; then this is `409 FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE`. The free alternatives are `POST /seo/backlinks/import` (a Search Console links export) and the Bing Webmaster Tools feed.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Give the person `error.approval.url`;\nonce they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`.\nThe approval is void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the\ndashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client."
  },
  {
    "id": "outreach",
    "title": "Outreach",
    "body": "# Outreach\n\nLink outreach, read only: readiness, the connected mailbox, contacts, campaigns and\nthreads. Contains personal data of people outside the organisation. Accepting the outreach\npolicy and connecting a mailbox are done by a person in the dashboard.\n\n## GET /outreach/readiness\n\nRead outreach readiness\n\nScope: outreach:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getOutreachReadiness\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nWhether this Site can send outreach, and if not, what is missing, as sentences a person acts on\n(`next_steps`): the outreach policy an owner accepts, the identity check, the plan, and the\nmailbox. Also this month's sending allowance and counts of contacts, campaigns and replies.\n\nAccepting the policy and connecting a mailbox are never done through the API: a person does both\nat https://app.writavo.com/outreach.\n\n## GET /outreach/mailbox\n\nRead the outreach mailbox\n\nScope: outreach:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getOutreachMailbox\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe customer's own mailbox outreach is sent from: its address, status, daily cap and sending\nwindow, and whether replies can be detected. Server names and credentials are never returned.\n`404` when no mailbox is connected; a person connects one at https://app.writavo.com/outreach.\n\n## GET /outreach/contacts\n\nList outreach contacts\n\nScope: outreach:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listOutreachContacts\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nPeople found for link outreach, newest first, each with where the address was found\n(`provenance`) and whether they unsubscribed or bounced. Contains personal data of people outside the organisation. Show it to the person; do not copy it elsewhere.\n\n## GET /outreach/campaigns\n\nList outreach campaigns\n\nScope: outreach:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listOutreachCampaigns\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe Site's outreach campaigns with their status, daily cap and step subjects. Message bodies and\nthe postal address are not returned. Contains personal data of people outside the organisation. Show it to the person; do not copy it elsewhere.\n\n## GET /outreach/threads\n\nList outreach threads\n\nScope: outreach:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listOutreachThreads\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nOne row per contact in a campaign, newest first: which step it is on, when the next message is\ndue, and whether they replied or the link was won. Message bodies are not available through the\nAPI. Contains personal data of people outside the organisation. Show it to the person; do not copy it elsewhere."
  },
  {
    "id": "team",
    "title": "Team",
    "body": "# Team\n\nMembers, invites, roles and permissions. Every change needs a person's approval when an AI\nagent asks, and an agent can never change the access of the person it acts for, nor\nanything to do with ownership.\n\n## GET /team/members\n\nList team members\n\nScope: team:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listTeamMembers\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nEveryone in the organisation that owns this Site, with their role. `is_you` marks the person the\nkey acts for. Contains the members' email addresses.\n\n## GET /team/members/{user_id}\n\nRead one team member\n\nScope: team:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getTeamMember\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nOne member, with the live API keys they created (`live_api_keys`). Those keys are what block\nremoving them: a person revokes or reassigns them in Settings > API keys first. Not a member is\n`404`.\n\n## PATCH /team/members/{user_id}\n\nChange a member's role\n\nScope: team:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateMemberRole\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nChange a member's role to `admin`, `editor` or `viewer`. The role decides what they can do on\nevery Site in the organisation, unless individual permissions override it\n(`GET /team/members/{user_id}/permissions`).\n\nAn admin can change editors and viewers; only an owner can make or change an admin. A change\nthe caller's own role does not allow is `403 FORBIDDEN` with the reason. An AI agent can never change the access of the person it acts for, nor anything to do with ownership: a target that is that person, or an owner, is `403 FORBIDDEN` before any approval is asked, and the message names who can do it in the dashboard (https://app.writavo.com/team). The approval itself can only be given by the person whose assistant asked, never by the member it affects.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it changes who can do what in the organisation. Give the person\n`error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval:\n<error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the request would do changes before the\nretry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## DELETE /team/members/{user_id}\n\nRemove a team member\n\nScope: team:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"removeTeamMember\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nRemove someone from the organisation. They lose access to every Site in it at once. A member who\nstill owns live API keys is `409 CONFLICT` (\"This member still owns N live API key(s). A person\nrevokes or reassigns them in Settings > API keys first.\"). An AI agent can never change the access of the person it acts for, nor anything to do with ownership: a target that is that person, or an owner, is `403 FORBIDDEN` before any approval is asked, and the message names who can do it in the dashboard (https://app.writavo.com/team). The approval itself can only be given by the person whose assistant asked, never by the member it affects.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it changes who can do what in the organisation. Give the person\n`error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval:\n<error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the request would do changes before the\nretry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /team/members/{user_id}/permissions\n\nRead a member's permissions\n\nScope: team:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getMemberPermissions\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nEvery permission, whether this member has it, and why: an individual override, their role's\nsetting in this organisation, or the platform default.\n\n## PATCH /team/members/{user_id}/permissions\n\nChange a member's permissions\n\nScope: roles:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateMemberPermissions\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nGrant or revoke individual permissions for one member, on top of their role, or clear an\noverride (`effect: null`) so the role decides again. Up to 20 changes, applied all or nothing.\nEach change must be a permission the caller holds, not a protected one, for a member whose role\nthe caller may manage; otherwise the whole request is `403 FORBIDDEN` naming the first problem.\nAn AI agent can never change the access of the person it acts for, nor anything to do with ownership: a target that is that person, or an owner, is `403 FORBIDDEN` before any approval is asked, and the message names who can do it in the dashboard (https://app.writavo.com/team). The approval itself can only be given by the person whose assistant asked, never by the member it affects.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it changes who can do what in the organisation. Give the person\n`error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval:\n<error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the request would do changes before the\nretry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /team/invites\n\nList pending invites\n\nScope: team:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listTeamInvites\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nInvitations that have not been accepted yet, with their role and expiry. Accepted invites are\nnot listed; expired ones are, with `status: expired`.\n\n## POST /team/invites\n\nInvite someone to the organisation\n\nScope: team:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"inviteTeamMember\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nInvite someone by email as `admin`, `editor` or `viewer`. Writavo does not email them: the\nresponse carries `accept_url`, a single-use link valid for 7 days. Give it to the person to\nforward to the invitee; it is shown once, and a retry with the same `Idempotency-Key` returns the\ninvite without it.\n\nEach member is a seat, billed pay-as-you-go past the included allowance; with no card on file\nthat is `402 PAYMENT_METHOD_REQUIRED`, and the message carries the link where the person adds one\n(https://app.writavo.com/billing?action=add-card). A pending invite for the same email, or someone already a\nmember, is `409 CONFLICT`. Inviting an owner is `403 FORBIDDEN`: ownership changes hands only in\nthe dashboard. The approval can only be given by the person whose assistant asked.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it changes who can do what in the organisation. Give the person\n`error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval:\n<error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the request would do changes before the\nretry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## DELETE /team/invites/{id}\n\nRevoke an invite\n\nScope: team:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"revokeTeamInvite\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nCancel a pending invite, so its link stops working. Only reduces access, so it is never asked\nfor approval.\n\n## GET /team/roles\n\nRead what each role can do\n\nScope: team:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getRoleMatrix\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nFor the `admin`, `editor` and `viewer` roles, every permission and whether the role has it in\nthis organisation, and whether that is the organisation's own setting or the platform default.\nOwners always have every permission.\n\n## PATCH /team/roles/{role}\n\nChange what a role can do\n\nScope: roles:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateRolePermissions\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nGrant or revoke permissions for everyone with a role in this organisation, or reset one to the\nplatform default (`granted: null`). Up to 20 changes. The caller may only change a role below\ntheir own, and only permissions they hold themselves; the role of the person the key acts for is\n`403 FORBIDDEN`, because an AI agent can never change the access of the person it acts for. The approval can only be given by the person whose assistant asked.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it changes who can do what in the organisation. Give the person\n`error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval:\n<error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the request would do changes before the\nretry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## GET /team/permissions\n\nList the permission catalog\n\nScope: team:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listPermissionCatalog\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nEvery permission that exists, with its label, what it allows, its category, the lowest role it\ncan be given to, and whether it is protected (cannot be granted individually)."
  },
  {
    "id": "billing",
    "title": "Billing",
    "body": "# Billing\n\nThe plan, credit balance, allowances, overage estimate, invoices, credit packs, auto-refill\nand the Site's credit cap. Payment details and plan changes are never taken here: they are\nlinks a person opens.\n\n## GET /billing\n\nRead the billing summary\n\nScope: billing:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getBillingSummary\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe whole billing picture in one read: the plan and any scheduled change, whether a card is on\nfile, the credit balance, the CMS overage so far this period, auto-refill, this Site's credit cap,\nand every allowance with what has been used.\n\nCMS allowances (`is_payg: true`) are pay-as-you-go and identical on every plan: going past one\nbills the overage and never blocks. Never call them plan limits and never suggest upgrading to\nlift one.\n\n## GET /billing/invoices\n\nList invoices and payments\n\nScope: billing:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listInvoices\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nInvoices, credit pack purchases and refunds, newest first, with links to the hosted invoice and\nits PDF. Page back with `before` (the `next_cursor` of the previous page). The list is read from\nWritavo's own copy of the billing history; `stale: true` only says that copy has not been\nrefreshed recently, so the last few changes may not be in it yet.\n\n## GET /billing/credit-packs\n\nList credit packs\n\nScope: billing:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listCreditPacks\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe credit packs that can be bought on top of the plan's monthly credits, with their price.\n\n## POST /billing/credit-packs/{key}/checkout\n\nStart a credit pack purchase\n\nScope: billing:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"startCreditPurchase\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nReturns a Stripe Checkout link for one credit pack. Nothing is charged by this call: the person\nopens the link in their browser and pays on Stripe's page, and the credits arrive when the\npayment completes. That page is where they consent, so no approval is asked. Give them\n`checkout_url` exactly as returned; it is shown once. Card details never pass through the API or\nan assistant.\n\nAn unknown or inactive pack is `404`.\n\n## GET /billing/links\n\nGet the billing links for a person\n\nScope: billing:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getBillingLinks\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe dashboard pages where a person changes the plan, adds or changes a card, and sees invoices.\nThe API never changes the plan or takes payment details; give the person the right link.\n\n## POST /billing/scheduled-change/cancel\n\nKeep the current plan\n\nScope: billing:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"keepCurrentPlan\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nCancel a scheduled plan change (a downgrade or cancellation set for the end of the period), so\nthe organisation stays on its current plan and keeps paying for it. With nothing scheduled it\nanswers `released: false` and asks no approval.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Asked only when a plan change is\nactually scheduled. Give the person `error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the\nidentical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the\nrequest would do changes before the retry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the\nrequest comes from an MCP client.\n\n## PATCH /billing/autorefill\n\nChange auto-refill\n\nScope: billing:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateAutorefill\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nTurn auto-refill on or off, or change it. While on, the saved card is charged for `pack_key`\nwhenever the credit balance falls to `threshold_credits`, never more than `monthly_ceiling_usd`\na month. Turning it on needs `pack_key` and `monthly_ceiling_usd` (`422` otherwise; a ceiling\nbelow the pack's price is also `422`) and a card on file: without one it is\n`409 PREREQUISITE_MISSING`, and the person adds a card at\nhttps://app.writavo.com/billing?action=add-card. Turning it off is never asked and never charges.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Asked only when auto-refill is on\nafter the change; turning it off is never asked. Give the person `error.approval.url`; once they\napprove, repeat the identical request with `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`. The approval\nis void if what the request would do changes before the retry. A key made in the dashboard is\nasked only when the request comes from an MCP client.\n\n## PATCH /billing/site-credit-cap\n\nChange this Site's credit cap\n\nScope: billing:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: run_writavo_action with operation_id \"updateSiteCreditCap\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nSet the most credits this Site may spend in a month, independent of the organisation's balance;\n`null` removes the cap. Lowering it, or capping an uncapped Site, only reduces what can be spent\nand is never asked. The cap is what answers `402 SPEND_CAP_REACHED`.\n\n**When an AI agent asks.** A key from a device or OAuth sign-in, or any request from an MCP\nclient, always gets `428 APPROVAL_REQUIRED` on the first try, whatever the organisation's\napprovals switch says, because it spends money or credits. Asked only when the cap is raised or\nremoved. Give the person `error.approval.url`; once they approve, repeat the identical request\nwith `Writavo-Approval: <error.approval.id>`. The approval is void if what the request would do\nchanges before the retry. A key made in the dashboard is asked only when the request comes from\nan MCP client."
  },
  {
    "id": "insights",
    "title": "Insights",
    "body": "# Insights\n\nReports and logs: the Site overview, costs per Site and per article, taxonomy counts,\nfunction logs, the audit log and the AI agent call log.\n\n## GET /insights/overview\n\nRead the Site overview\n\nScope: insights:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getSiteOverview\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nThe Site at a glance: the last 30 days of articles generated and published, images, reads, API\ncost and errors; how many articles are at each status; today's publishes; and the five most\nrecent pipeline runs.\n\n## GET /insights/costs\n\nRead the Site's costs\n\nScope: insights:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getSiteCosts\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nWhat the Site's AI and data work cost over a date range (by default the 30 days ending at `to`,\nwhich defaults to today), by pipeline stage and by provider, in US dollars.\n\n## GET /insights/articles/{id}/costs\n\nRead one article's costs\n\nScope: insights:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getArticleCosts\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nWhat one article cost to research, write, improve and illustrate, by stage and by provider.\nZero for an article written by hand.\n\n## GET /insights/taxonomy\n\nRead taxonomy counts\n\nScope: insights:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"getTaxonomyCounts\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nEvery category, tag and author with how many articles use it. A quick way to find empty or\noverloaded ones.\n\n## GET /logs/functions\n\nRead the Site's function logs\n\nScope: logs:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listFunctionLogs\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nLog lines the pipeline and the Site's background jobs wrote for this Site, newest first.\nFilter by `level` or `function_name`. Platform-wide lines are never included.\n\n## GET /logs/audit\n\nRead the audit log\n\nScope: logs:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listAuditLog\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nWho changed what on this Site and in its organisation, newest first: the action, the target, the\nperson, and the API key when the change came through the API. Filter by an `action` prefix such\nas `billing.` or `team.`.\n\n## GET /logs/agent-calls\n\nRead the AI agent call log\n\nScope: logs:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: read_writavo_action with operation_id \"listAgentCalls\" (find it with search_writavo_actions).\n\nEvery request an AI agent key made on this Site, refusals included, newest first: the app, the\ntool, the operation, the outcome, how long it took, and the approval it used. Kept for 90 days."
  },
  {
    "id": "api-keys",
    "title": "API keys",
    "body": "# API keys\n\nKey management. Specified here, implemented in API-2.\n\nNot available as tools. Credential management stays in the dashboard. A server that can mint a secret key is a server whose compromise mints secret keys, and the key it would use to do so is sitting in a config file on the same machine.\n\n## GET /keys\n\nList API keys\n\nScope: keys:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nMetadata only. The secret itself is shown once, at creation, and is never retrievable\nafterwards because only a hash is stored. `key_prefix` is the displayable fragment you\nuse to tell keys apart.\n\nRequires a secret key carrying `keys:read`. A publishable key can never read this.\n\n## POST /keys\n\nCreate an API key\n\nScope: keys:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nReturns the secret exactly once, in `data.secret`. Store it immediately. There is no way\nto recover it later, and support cannot retrieve it for you.\n\nA key can never be created with more authority than its creator has. The scopes you\nrequest are intersected with the creator's own permissions, and the granted set comes\nback in `data.scopes`. If you asked for something you do not hold, the key is still\ncreated, without it. Compare what you asked for against what you got.\n\nA secret key's authority is also re-evaluated on every request against its creator's\nlive permissions, so revoking a person's access immediately narrows every key they made.\n\n**A retry does not give you the secret again.** `Idempotency-Key` guarantees you created\none key rather than two, and a replayed response returns the key's `id`, `kind`,\n`key_prefix` and `scopes` with `secret: null` and `secret_replayable: false`. The secret\nis never stored anywhere, including in the idempotency record, because storing it would\nput a live credential in a database backup. If you lost it, rotate the key.\n\n## POST /keys/{id}/rotate\n\nRotate an API key\n\nScope: keys:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nIssues a new secret for the same key record, keeping its name, and returns it once.\n\nOnly the person who created the key, an organisation owner or a platform admin may rotate\nit: a rotation hands over a live credential that keeps acting with its creator's\npermissions. Anyone else with `api_keys.manage` gets `403 INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE`. The new\nsecret's scopes are the old key's scopes limited to what the caller could grant today, and\na rotation that would leave no scopes is refused with `403 INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE`.\n\nAs with creation, a replayed retry returns `secret: null` and `secret_replayable: false`\nrather than handing out the credential a second time. Rotate again if you lost it.\n\nSet `grace_seconds` to keep the old secret working while you deploy the new one. During\nthe grace window both work. After it, the old one returns `401 API_KEY_REVOKED`. A grace\nof `0` cuts the old secret off immediately, which is the right choice if you are rotating\nbecause it leaked.\n\n## DELETE /keys/{id}\n\nRevoke an API key\n\nScope: keys:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nImmediate and permanent. The key record is kept, marked revoked, so the audit trail\nsurvives, but the secret stops working at once and returns `401 API_KEY_REVOKED`.\n\nRevoking the key you are calling with is allowed. It is the last request that key makes."
  },
  {
    "id": "webhooks",
    "title": "Webhooks",
    "body": "# Webhooks\n\nOutbound event delivery. Register an HTTPS endpoint, subscribe it to events, and receive a\nsigned POST whenever your content changes, from this API or from the dashboard.\n\nNot available as tools. Account configuration, not content. An assistant that can repoint delivery URLs can quietly redirect a Site's event stream, and that is a change a person should make deliberately.\n\n## GET /webhooks\n\nList webhook endpoints\n\nScope: webhooks:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\n\n\n## POST /webhooks\n\nCreate a webhook endpoint\n\nScope: webhooks:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nRegisters a URL to receive signed event deliveries. The signing secret is returned once,\nat creation, and never again: record it before you close the response. If you lose it,\n`POST /webhooks/{id}/rotate-secret` issues a new one.\n\nVerify every delivery, using the recipe at the top of this section, before you parse the\nbody.\n\nThe URL must be public HTTPS. Private, loopback, link-local and metadata addresses are\nrefused, and so is a hostname that resolves to one, at save time and again at delivery\ntime. A webhook cannot be pointed at internal infrastructure.\n\nDelivery is at least once. Retries use exponential backoff, and an endpoint that keeps\nfailing is disabled automatically and reported to you. Deduplicate on the payload's `id`\nand make your handler idempotent.\n\nA Site may register at most ten endpoints.\n\n## GET /webhooks/{id}\n\nRead one webhook endpoint\n\nScope: webhooks:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\n\n\n## PATCH /webhooks/{id}\n\nUpdate a webhook endpoint\n\nScope: webhooks:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nChange the URL, the subscribed events, or re-enable an endpoint that was auto-disabled\nafter repeated failures. Re-enabling does not replay what you missed.\n\n## DELETE /webhooks/{id}\n\nDelete a webhook endpoint\n\nScope: webhooks:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nDeliveries stop at once. Queued retries for this endpoint are dropped.\n\n## POST /webhooks/{id}/rotate-secret\n\nRotate the signing secret\n\nScope: webhooks:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nIssues a new signing secret and returns it once. The old secret stops working\nimmediately: there is no grace window, because a window in which two secrets both\nvalidate is a window in which a leaked secret still works.\n\nDeliveries sent between the rotation and your receiver being updated will fail\nverification. They are retried on the normal backoff, so update the receiver promptly and\nthe queue drains itself.\n\n## GET /webhooks/{id}/deliveries\n\nList deliveries for an endpoint\n\nScope: webhooks:read. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nThe delivery log, newest first. Use it to answer \"did you send it and did we accept it\".\n`response_status` is what your server returned; `attempt` counts from 1 to 6.\n\nThere is one row per ATTEMPT, and every attempt of one event shares its `event_id`. A row\nwith `status: failed` and `exhausted: false` will be retried; `exhausted: true` means the\nladder gave up.\n\n## POST /webhooks/{id}/deliveries/{delivery_id}/redeliver\n\nSend one delivery again\n\nScope: webhooks:write. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none.\n\nQueues the same event for delivery again, with the same `event_id` and byte-identical\nbody, so your handler sees it as the event it already knows how to deduplicate rather\nthan as a second, different fact. Use it after fixing a receiver that was down.\n\nThe attempt counter starts again at 1: this is a fresh ladder you asked for, not a\ncontinuation of the one that failed. The endpoint must be enabled."
  },
  {
    "id": "device-sign-in",
    "title": "Device sign-in",
    "body": "# Device sign-in\n\nDevice sign-in for command line tools and MCP clients: a person approves access in the\ndashboard instead of copying a key. The only endpoints that take no API key.\n\n## POST /auth/device\n\nStart a device sign-in\n\nScope: none. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none. Covered by login.\n\nStarts a sign-in for a command line tool or MCP client, modelled on the OAuth device\nauthorization grant (RFC 8628). Takes no API key: this is how a client comes to have one.\n\n**The client generates the key.** Create a secret the same shape as ours, `wv_sk_`\nfollowed by 32 base64url characters (24 random bytes), keep it private, and send only its\nSHA-256 as `key_hash` plus its first 12 characters as `key_prefix`. The secret never\nleaves your machine; approval registers its hash as an ordinary secret key.\n\nShow the person `verification_uri_complete` (or `verification_uri` and `user_code`). They\nsign in to the dashboard, or create an account first, choose a Site, and approve. Then\npoll `POST /auth/device/token` every `interval` seconds until it says `approved`, and\nstart using your key. The request expires after `expires_in` seconds.\n\nThe key is created for the approving person, on the Site they choose, with the scopes you\nasked for that they are allowed to grant, and expires after 90 days. It appears under\nSettings > API keys, where it can be revoked like any other.\n\n`flow: \"oauth\"` is reserved for Writavo's own hosted MCP server, which runs this sign-in\non a person's behalf behind its OAuth consent. Sent by anything else it is refused with\n`403 FORBIDDEN`: leave `flow` out.\n\n## POST /auth/device/token\n\nPoll a device sign-in\n\nScope: none. Publishable key: no. Spends credits: no.\nTool: none. Covered by login.\n\nReports whether the person has approved the sign-in. It returns an outcome, never a\ncredential: on `approved`, the key you generated is live, and the response says which\nSite it belongs to, which scopes it carries and when it expires.\n\n`pending` means keep waiting. `slow_down` means you polled faster than `interval`; wait\nthe `interval` it returns before the next poll. `denied` and `expired` are final: start\nagain with a new key."
  },
  {
    "id": "tools",
    "title": "What this server exposes",
    "body": "# Tools\n\nEvery tool below is compiled from the same specification this reference is generated from, so a tool cannot describe an endpoint that does not exist and cannot accept a field the API refuses.\n\n- verify_api_key: GET /ping\n- get_site_info: GET /site\n- get_content_types: GET /content-types\n- get_usage: GET /usage\n- list_articles: GET /articles\n- create_article: POST /articles\n- get_article: GET /articles/{id}\n- update_article: PATCH /articles/{id}\n- delete_article: DELETE /articles/{id} (asks you first)\n- publish_article: POST /articles/{id}/publish (asks you first)\n- unpublish_article: POST /articles/{id}/unpublish (asks you first)\n- schedule_article: POST /articles/{id}/schedule (asks you first)\n- cancel_article_schedule: POST /articles/{id}/cancel-schedule\n- list_categories: GET /categories\n- create_category: POST /categories\n- get_category: GET /categories/{id}\n- update_category: PATCH /categories/{id}\n- delete_category: DELETE /categories/{id} (asks you first)\n- list_tags: GET /tags\n- create_tag: POST /tags\n- get_tag: GET /tags/{id}\n- update_tag: PATCH /tags/{id}\n- delete_tag: DELETE /tags/{id} (asks you first)\n- list_authors: GET /authors\n- create_author: POST /authors\n- get_author: GET /authors/{id}\n- update_author: PATCH /authors/{id}\n- delete_author: DELETE /authors/{id} (asks you first)\n- list_media: GET /media\n- get_media: GET /media/{id}\n- update_media: PATCH /media/{id}\n- delete_media: DELETE /media/{id} (asks you first)\n- list_pipeline_runs: GET /pipeline/runs\n- trigger_pipeline_run: POST /pipeline/runs (asks you first)\n- get_pipeline_status: GET /pipeline/runs/{id}\n- get_pipeline_queue: GET /pipeline/queue\n- upload_media: Upload an image and register it in the media library, in one call.\n- get_api_docs: Read the API reference offline. One of the few tools that needs no key.\n- login: Sign in through the browser: a person approves, and a key generated on this machine goes live.\n- login_status: Check whether a sign-in started with login has been approved, and which Site it is for.\n- logout: Sign out on this machine: revoke the signed-in key on the server, then forget it locally.\n- start_plan_purchase: Get the dashboard link to choose a plan. Payment happens on Stripe's page, never in the chat.\n- import_content: Import articles from a Writavo import file: dry run first, then create, re-host images and publish with original dates.\n- search_writavo_actions: Find the operation for a settings, delivery, SEO, team, billing or insights task, with its input schema and whether it needs approval or costs money.\n- read_writavo_action: Run one READ operation found with search_writavo_actions (settings, SEO, team, billing, insights). Changes nothing.\n- run_writavo_action: Run one operation that CHANGES something, found with search_writavo_actions, validated against its schema, with the same confirmation and approval steps as every other tool.\n\n## Actions (search_writavo_actions, then run_writavo_action)\n\nSettings, delivery, SEO, the team, billing and insights are not separate tools. Find the operation with search_writavo_actions (a few words, optionally an area), then call read_writavo_action (for a GET, which changes nothing) or run_writavo_action (for everything else) with its operation_id and arguments. Confirmation and approval work exactly as they do for every other tool.\n\n- createContentType (formats_and_prompts, run): POST /content-types\n- createPlanItem (pipeline, run): POST /pipeline/queue\n- getPipelineConfig (pipeline, read): GET /pipeline/config\n- updatePipelineConfig (pipeline, run): PATCH /pipeline/config (spends credits, asks you first)\n- reorderPlanItems (pipeline, run): POST /pipeline/queue/reorder\n- getPlanItem (pipeline, read): GET /pipeline/queue/{id}\n- updatePlanItem (pipeline, run): PATCH /pipeline/queue/{id}\n- deletePlanItem (pipeline, run): DELETE /pipeline/queue/{id} (asks you first)\n- requeueArticle (pipeline, run): POST /pipeline/articles/{id}/requeue (spends credits, asks you first)\n- listPrompts (formats_and_prompts, read): GET /pipeline/prompts\n- setPromptOverride (formats_and_prompts, run): PATCH /pipeline/prompts/{stage}\n- resetPrompt (formats_and_prompts, run): DELETE /pipeline/prompts/{stage} (asks you first)\n- getContentType (formats_and_prompts, read): GET /content-types/{id}\n- updateContentType (formats_and_prompts, run): PATCH /content-types/{id}\n- deleteContentType (formats_and_prompts, run): DELETE /content-types/{id} (asks you first)\n- getSiteSettings (site_settings, read): GET /site/settings\n- updateSiteSettings (site_settings, run): PATCH /site/settings\n- getKnowledgeProfile (site_settings, read): GET /site/knowledge-profile\n- updateKnowledgeProfile (site_settings, run): PATCH /site/knowledge-profile\n- getOrganisation (organisation, read): GET /organisation\n- renameOrganisation (organisation, run): PATCH /organisation\n- getDelivery (delivery, read): GET /delivery\n- setupReverseProxy (delivery, run): POST /delivery/proxy (asks you first)\n- getProxyInstallers (delivery, read): GET /delivery/proxy/installers\n- setupHeadlessDelivery (delivery, run): POST /delivery/headless\n- connectCustomDomain (delivery, run): POST /delivery/custom-domain (costs money, asks you first)\n- removeCustomDomain (delivery, run): DELETE /delivery/custom-domain (asks you first)\n- runDeliveryHealthCheck (delivery, run): POST /delivery/health-checks\n- getHostedSite (delivery, read): GET /delivery/hosted-site\n- updateHostedSiteBranding (delivery, run): PATCH /delivery/hosted-site/branding\n- publishHostedSite (delivery, run): POST /delivery/hosted-site/publish (asks you first)\n- listCmsConnections (delivery, read): GET /delivery/cms\n- connectCms (delivery, run): POST /delivery/cms\n- disconnectCms (delivery, run): DELETE /delivery/cms/{provider} (asks you first)\n- pushToCms (delivery, run): POST /delivery/cms/push (asks you first)\n- listCmsPushLog (delivery, read): GET /delivery/cms/push-log\n- getSeoOverview (seo, read): GET /seo/overview\n- refreshSiteMetrics (seo, run): POST /seo/site-metrics/refresh (spends credits, asks you first)\n- listCompetitors (seo, read): GET /seo/competitors\n- addCompetitor (seo, run): POST /seo/competitors\n- updateCompetitor (seo, run): PATCH /seo/competitors/{id}\n- removeCompetitor (seo, run): DELETE /seo/competitors/{id} (asks you first)\n- listTrackedKeywords (seo, read): GET /seo/keywords\n- trackKeyword (seo, run): POST /seo/keywords\n- updateTrackedKeyword (seo, run): PATCH /seo/keywords/{id}\n- untrackKeyword (seo, run): DELETE /seo/keywords/{id} (asks you first)\n- getKeywordHistory (seo, read): GET /seo/keywords/{id}/history\n- listKeywordAlerts (seo, read): GET /seo/keyword-alerts\n- acknowledgeKeywordAlerts (seo, run): POST /seo/keyword-alerts/acknowledge\n- runRankCheck (seo, run): POST /seo/rank-check (costs money, asks you first)\n- listContentGaps (seo, read): GET /seo/content-gaps\n- scanContentGaps (seo, run): POST /seo/content-gaps/scan (spends credits, asks you first)\n- updateContentGap (seo, run): PATCH /seo/content-gaps/{id}\n- planContentGap (seo, run): POST /seo/content-gaps/{id}/plan\n- getInternalLinkHealth (seo, read): GET /seo/internal-links\n- rescanInternalLinks (seo, run): POST /seo/internal-links/rescan\n- listLlmMentions (seo, read): GET /seo/llm-mentions\n- checkLlmMentions (seo, run): POST /seo/llm-mentions/check (spends credits, asks you first)\n- getEngagement (seo, read): GET /seo/engagement\n- getBacklinkOverview (seo, read): GET /seo/backlinks/overview\n- listBacklinks (seo, read): GET /seo/backlinks\n- scanBacklinkProfile (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/scan (spends credits, asks you first)\n- pullBacklinkDetail (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/detail-pull (spends credits, asks you first)\n- listDisavowEntries (seo, read): GET /seo/backlinks/disavow\n- addDisavowEntry (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/disavow\n- removeDisavowEntry (seo, run): DELETE /seo/backlinks/disavow/{id} (asks you first)\n- getDisavowFile (seo, read): GET /seo/backlinks/disavow-file\n- importBacklinksCsv (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/import\n- verifyBacklinks (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/verify\n- connectBing (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/bing\n- syncBing (seo, run): POST /seo/backlinks/bing/sync\n- listLinkOpportunities (seo, read): GET /seo/link-opportunities\n- addLinkOpportunity (seo, run): POST /seo/link-opportunities\n- updateLinkOpportunity (seo, run): PATCH /seo/link-opportunities/{id}\n- planLinkOpportunity (seo, run): POST /seo/link-opportunities/{id}/plan\n- scanLinkIntersect (seo, run): POST /seo/link-opportunities/intersect-scan (spends credits, asks you first)\n- getOutreachReadiness (outreach, read): GET /outreach/readiness\n- getOutreachMailbox (outreach, read): GET /outreach/mailbox\n- listOutreachContacts (outreach, read): GET /outreach/contacts\n- listOutreachCampaigns (outreach, read): GET /outreach/campaigns\n- listOutreachThreads (outreach, read): GET /outreach/threads\n- listTeamMembers (team, read): GET /team/members\n- getTeamMember (team, read): GET /team/members/{user_id}\n- updateMemberRole (team, run): PATCH /team/members/{user_id} (asks you first)\n- removeTeamMember (team, run): DELETE /team/members/{user_id} (asks you first)\n- getMemberPermissions (team, read): GET /team/members/{user_id}/permissions\n- updateMemberPermissions (team, run): PATCH /team/members/{user_id}/permissions (asks you first)\n- listTeamInvites (team, read): GET /team/invites\n- inviteTeamMember (team, run): POST /team/invites (asks you first)\n- revokeTeamInvite (team, run): DELETE /team/invites/{id} (asks you first)\n- getRoleMatrix (team, read): GET /team/roles\n- updateRolePermissions (team, run): PATCH /team/roles/{role} (asks you first)\n- listPermissionCatalog (team, read): GET /team/permissions\n- getBillingSummary (billing, read): GET /billing\n- listInvoices (billing, read): GET /billing/invoices\n- listCreditPacks (billing, read): GET /billing/credit-packs\n- startCreditPurchase (billing, run): POST /billing/credit-packs/{key}/checkout\n- getBillingLinks (billing, read): GET /billing/links\n- keepCurrentPlan (billing, run): POST /billing/scheduled-change/cancel (costs money, asks you first)\n- updateAutorefill (billing, run): PATCH /billing/autorefill (costs money, asks you first)\n- updateSiteCreditCap (billing, run): PATCH /billing/site-credit-cap (asks you first)\n- getSiteOverview (insights, read): GET /insights/overview\n- getSiteCosts (insights, read): GET /insights/costs\n- getArticleCosts (insights, read): GET /insights/articles/{id}/costs\n- getTaxonomyCounts (insights, read): GET /insights/taxonomy\n- listFunctionLogs (insights, read): GET /logs/functions\n- listAuditLog (insights, read): GET /logs/audit\n- listAgentCalls (insights, read): GET /logs/agent-calls\n\n## What it deliberately cannot do\n\n### API keys\n\nCredential management stays in the dashboard. A server that can mint a secret key is a server whose compromise mints secret keys, and the key it would use to do so is sitting in a config file on the same machine.\n\n### Webhooks\n\nAccount configuration, not content. An assistant that can repoint delivery URLs can quietly redirect a Site's event stream, and that is a change a person should make deliberately.\n\n## Never through an AI agent\n\nWhatever permissions a connection carries, these stay with a person. Give them the next step exactly as written.\n\n### Change the AI agent switch, the approvals switch or the default permissions\n\nAn agent must not be able to switch off the controls that govern it. A person changes this at https://app.writavo.com/settings/agents.\n\n### Approve its own requests, or widen its own access\n\nAn approval is a person saying yes; an agent approving itself is no approval at all. The person approves at the link, or reconnects the assistant to choose more permissions.\n\n### Change the access of the person it acts for (their role, their permissions, their role's permissions)\n\nThat would be an agent widening its own access by another route. That person, or another owner or admin, does it at https://app.writavo.com/team.\n\n### Delete a Site or the organisation\n\nIrreversible, and it takes a live blog down for everyone. Not available to AI agents. The person contacts https://writavo.com/support.\n\n### Enter or change payment details\n\nCard details never pass through an AI assistant. Add or change a card at https://app.writavo.com/billing?action=add-card.\n\n### Change the plan\n\nA plan change is a purchase the person makes on Stripe's page. Get the plan link with start_plan_purchase (or https://app.writavo.com/billing) and give it to the person.\n\n### Transfer ownership or make anyone an owner\n\nOwnership is the last word on an organisation and changes hands only in person. The owner does it at https://app.writavo.com/team.\n\n### Accept the outreach policy, pass identity checks, or connect an outreach mailbox\n\nSending outreach is a legal commitment, and a mailbox password never passes through an AI assistant. An owner or a person with integrations access does it at https://app.writavo.com/outreach.\n\n### Enter a CMS or Bing Webmaster Tools credential\n\nThird party credentials never pass through an AI assistant. The connect actions return the dashboard page where the person pastes it (https://app.writavo.com/delivery).\n\n### Create, rotate or revoke API keys; manage webhooks\n\nA tool that can mint a credential is a tool whose compromise mints credentials. A person does this at https://app.writavo.com/settings/api-keys or https://app.writavo.com/settings/webhooks.\n\n### Anything that needs Writavo platform staff\n\nPlatform administration is not something an organisation or its agents can reach. Not something an organisation can change. The person contacts https://writavo.com/support."
  }
